  "catalogueCode": "OE-0247-b",
  "description": [
    {
      "value": "<p>A dense silicate world that was inside its star while that star was a red giant, and came out of it stripped, scorched and eventually frozen. The surface is glass over slumped rock, and about four metres of section records the entire event. Relict endolithic life survives eleven kilometres down, in pore water that was never heated past ninety degrees. On the available evidence it is the oldest continuously living thing the Consortium has anywhere on file.</p>",
      "inLanguage": [{ "id": ["core.peerdb.org", "LANGUAGE", "en-GB"] }]
    },
    {
      "value": "<p>Svet, ki ga je zvezda ob širjenju ožgala in je zdaj zmrznjen. Globoko spodaj je življenje preživelo.</p>",
      "inLanguage": [{ "id": ["core.peerdb.org", "LANGUAGE", "sl-SI"] }]
    }
  ],
